{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations","id":781297,"title":"Alternate Take on Abominations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-06T13:23:28-08:00","id":781297,"title":"Alternate Take on Abominations","content":"<i>WARNING: What you're about to read is extremely over-powered by PC standards and IS NOT MEANT FOR PLAYERS! These aren't &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;unbalanced&quot;. They're MEANT to be terrifying and have the ability to chew up neonates/whelps and spit them back out again. </i><br /> <br /> <b>What Was Wrong With the Old Abominations?</b><br /> <br /> The original abominations are designed to be pathetic, pitiable creatures that are werewolves first and vampires a distant second. Basically, the rules do everything in their power to make these creatures \u201cunplayable\u201d to quell players from wanting to play this. This fits the darker, hopeless tone of the original World of Darkness, but I run the setting somewhat differently.<br /> Abominations should be exactly what their name implies: something to be terrified of, something so horrible, they need to be destroyed at all costs. But these are purely NPCs, they are not for players unless you want to run a VERY dark and unusual chronicle.<br /> <br /> What if a PC somehow becomes one during gameplay? Assuming you're foolish enough to ALLOW it, inform the player that they will INSTANTLY gain three flaws: Hunted (Garou), Hunted (Kindred), and Dark Fate. If they still insist,and you're insanely generous? To borrow a quote from an old friend, &quot;their deaths will be SPECTACULAR.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Where Do They Come From?</b><br /> <br /> Abominations are not born or Embraced. They were created by an unholy ritual that has long since been lost to time. In the 9<sup>th</sup> Century, House Tremere\u2019s leaders had transformed into the undead. Appalled at their current condition, the Council of Seven commissioned projects into finding ways to undo or at least ameliorate their cursed condition. Nearly all of them failed. All but one.<br /> <br /> Goratrix approached one of his still-mortal former apprentices and urged him to find a way to \u201cpurify\u201d this vampiric form, to remove its weaknesses. The mage, a dark figure with view ethics (much like his teacher), took it as a challenge. Relocating to a private workshop, some ways away from Ceoris, his research led him to the Garou of Eastern Europe. At first he relied on captured subjects, but his every experiment failed.<br /> <br /> But finally, one of his captives turned out to be quite willing to aid in his experiments, a young Metis named Mikhail, apparently being some kind of bastard offspring of some taboo union amongst the beasts, he was treated as less than nothing, and vengeance burned in his heart. He wanted the strength to tear apart his tormentors. The mage saw in him the will to survive a dangerous new technique he wanted to try.<br /> <br /> What exactly transpired isn\u2019t known. What is, is that the mage succeeded beyond his wildest dream. Unfortunately, his subject came out of the Embrace in a bestial frenzy. He tore apart the mage\u2019s assistants, human and vampire alike, and gutted the sorcerer. Realizing his mistake, he used the last moments of his life to seal the creature in the hidden laboratory. There the rampaging beast was trapped, slowly sinking into torpor.<br /> <br /> And there things might have ended, if some poor sods hadn\u2019t unleashed the damned creature centuries later. Now, he\u2019s awake and seeking a way to recreate the mage\u2019s work. His own Embrace is poisonous to most Garou, and he\u2019s yet to find a reliable way to create more of his kind. Still, rumor has it, he\u2019s managed to find one or two with the strength of rage and will to<br /> survive the Embrace.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers of the Abomination</b><br /> <br /> So what makes an Abomintion so terrifying? Well to borrow a line, they have all the strengths and none of the weaknesses of both clans.<br /> <br /> <b>Garou Heritage</b><br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b><br /> <br /> Rank is irrelevant to an Abomination. They can learn any level of Gift, provided they can find a Wyrm Spirit or Bane to teach it to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b><br /> <br /> An Abomination has no Tribe, or access to Tribal Gifts. At least not in the traditional sense. <br /> <br /> <b>Regeneration</b><br /> <br /> Despite their undead status, their regenerative ability somehow survived. Garou heal one level of bashing or lethal damage every turn. (Please note, I house ruled out the \u201cnot in breed form\u201d and \u201cmake a roll to heal in combat\u201d out for regular old Garou as well). <b>Gifts of the Garou</b><br /> <br /> Gifts occupy an odd place. An Abomination has no tribe or kin to call upon, and most spirits flee at the sight of them. So a freshly Embraced Abomination loses access to his original Gifts. That is, until, they make contact with the darker elements of the spirit world. Corrupt things called Wyrm Spirits by the Garou are drawn to the Abominations, and through them, they can take a new personal Totem and find spirits willing to teach them dark and unholy Gifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Form</b><br /> <br /> An Abomination can change form like any other Garou. The bonuses stack with any received from Kindred Disciplines and spending Blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Rage &amp; Gnosis</b><br /> <br /> Rage and Gnosis remain largely unchanged. Gnosis is more difficult to regain and increase, however. They can both be used for more than just Garou abilities now, however Rage continues to be the fuel that drives their Garou side physically. It can also power physical Disciplines (Celerity, Potence, Fortitude) in place of Blood. In addition, Abominations can regain Rage by relenting to a Frenzy check.<br /> <br /> An Abomination can still access the mana of Gaia, but only through the blessings of the Wyrm. The Abomination must have a Totem background of at least 3 dots to be able to drain Gnosis from corrupted Cairns and other dark places. Pure Gnosis must be twisted first by a Rite before the Abomination can draw upon it. Until the Abomination has a personal Totem, they cannot increase permanent Gnosis with experience.<br /> <br /> Gnosis is the fuel of magic, and it is corrupted within an Abomination. As such, they can spend Gnosis in place of Blood to fuel the Blood Magic Disciplines, such as Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, Koldunic Sorcery, and their brethren.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Heritage</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b><br /> <br /> True Abominations are a small and very rare Bloodline descended from the Tremere, though only a handful are aware of this fact. Mikhail dubbed his line \u201cStrigoi\u201d based off a word from his homeland, meaning \u201cnightmare\u201d. In the half-millenium he\u2019s been active, Mikhail has managed to successfully create only six progeny. Four are believed to have been hunted down and killed.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline: Strigoi (Romanian for Nightmare)</b><br /> <br /> <i>In-Clan Disciplines:</i> Animalism, Dominate, Thaumaturgy (Spirit Manipulation [Guide to the Camarilla, Revised, pg. 106-107] is the default path, not Blood)<br /> <br /> <i>Clan Weakness:</i> Strigoi cannot create more of their own reliably. Any attempt to Embrace a human, fails. On occasion, however, if a Garou or kinfolk is chosen and prepared with certain mystical rituals, there is a chance, that they can survive the Embrace with an extended Willpower check (difficulty 9, minimum, over the course of 10 turns, minimum 5 successes). Success means Embrace, and rising as an Abomination. Failure means a quick, painful, screaming death. A Botch means the death is slow, and even more painful.<br /> <br /> <b>Paths</b><br /> <br /> An Abomination can follow any Path he chooses, though Mikhail follows a dark, twisted variant of Path of the Feral Heart. (To be fleshed out later).<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b><br /> <br /> An Abomination can learn Disciplines like any vampire. As mentioned above, Rage can be used in place of Blood for Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude. Gnosis can be spent in place of Blood when using Thaumaturgy and Necromancy (and the many variants).<br /> <br /> <b>Generation</b><br /> <br /> Generation remains unchanged. Given the first Strigoi\u2019s low Generation, any created from him would be equally low. Same goes for Blood Potency, if you\u2019re integrating it, per my other house rules.<br /> <br /> <b>The Banes of Existence</b><br /> <br /> If all this wasn\u2019t bad enough, the Abomination can now mockingly laugh at the things its progenitor species fear.<br /> <br /> Silver. Damage dependent on weapon type.<br /> <br /> Fire. Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Sunlight. Nothing. Absolutely nothing.<br /> <br /> The only sources of Aggravated damage are from mystical attacks that would rend the flesh of any creature. If the attack\u2019s source of damage is dependent on one of the banes, even in a mystical sense, (enchanted silver blade, Path of Flame, etc) then it deals Lethal damage instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:42:58-08:00","id":781462,"title":"","content":"I like it, might have to snag this if I ever get a game together","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T03:33:56-08:00","id":781631,"title":"","content":"Fair enough if it works for you and your campaign. But to me, it smells radically of cheese. Without any of the weaknesses of being a Vampire, it may as well just be a Metis Garou with Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T05:39:43-08:00","id":781666,"title":"","content":"Well... it's cool, really.<br /> But I'd prefer to see the Strigoi as another strain of Abominations, besides the official ones, rather then the only Abomination. That would be cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:11:25-08:00","id":781674,"title":"","content":"Where is the drawback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:53:20-08:00","id":781685,"title":"","content":"Doesn't fire deal aggravated damage to werewolves too? It should probably deal aggravated damage to these guys if it does to both parent species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3527-sidhe_blooded","name":"sidhe_blooded","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:24:45-08:00","id":781693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sidhe_blooded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781685#post781685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't fire deal aggravated damage to werewolves too? It should probably deal aggravated damage to these guys if it does to both parent species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The only time that Garou and Fera are more resistant to fire is when they used a Gift to effect this, though one of those, Master of Fire, is rather easy to acquire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:49:36-08:00","id":781695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sidhe_blooded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781685#post781685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't fire deal aggravated damage to werewolves too? It should probably deal aggravated damage to these guys if it does to both parent species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. For people who run a standard WoD game, fire should be Aggravated damage. I do not treat fire as Aggravated damage for any supernatural creature, when I'm running my Homewbrew WoD setting. As a consequence, , I tweak most Sabbat fire rituals to be about taunting the sun instead. Sorry, sidetrack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough if it works for you and your campaign. But to me, it smells radically of cheese.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cheese&quot; is matter of taste, but I can see why you'd call it that. As I said in my initial warning, this is meant to be overpowered and pants-wetting for anyone actually bumping into one in a Chronicle. I want a damned creature that is a boogeyman to Kindred and Garou alike. Something that at the end of the day, they'd join forces without a second thought to hunt down. And something like that has to be POWERFUL. I know that's a 4-letter word in WoD, but that's why its an ALTERNATE take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'd prefer to see the Strigoi as another strain of Abominations, besides the official ones, rather then the only Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy enough. There's no reason the two can't co-exist side by side. In fact, one of the plot points for the Chronicle I made thise creatures for, is that one day Mikhail finds a way to &quot;upgrade&quot; existing Abominations into Strigoi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the drawback?</div> </div> </div> </div>They cannot mass produce. Even reproduction is near-impossible. They number less than the modern Salubri Healers. Each one is a rarity, a boogeyman akin to the Nictuku (before V20DA at least). They are hunted by EVERYONE, should one be outed. If you're asking for some crippling weakness that makes them cursed, pitiable monsters that should seek self-destruction, well, you've got the RAW Abominations for that.<br /> <br /> They're in the same category as Strix, Nictuku, or Oracles. Yes, they exist. But you don't let players PLAY them, do you?<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you're wondering why I'd make rules for them, then, it's because I demand internal consistency between my PCs and NPCs. I build them as normal, determine how much advancement they'd accrue based on how long they've been active, and what they're doing and increase their power accordingly. If I need something even more powerful than that, I then add on ways they could have bucked the curb, through diablerie, mystical artifacts, or some special gift they already posses. If I need a unique sentient adversary, I find a way to create a character creation template, like above.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying NPCs can't break the rules, but when you have clearly defined limits and rules set, you can more easily tell when it'you're bending the rules in the name of good drama, or if you're just being cheesy and unfair with a pet NPC.\\<br /> <br /> I'm a writer at heart, and one of the things that drives me nuts about fiction, be it written or visual, is when supernatural powers have no governing principles to them, that they're just Deus Ex Machina for the writer to use, like technobabble in Star Trek. It's one of the reasons I've struggled so long with Mage the Ascension. It has rules, but its so... free form in its execution I've for years had incredible difficulty wrapping my head around magical styles and how to play one.<br /> <br /> I'm ashamed to say, the few times I've tried playing a mage, I've limited my spheres known to no more than my Arete rating so i can just ditch foci entirely and run them more like psychic manipulation than proper magick. Fortunately, I've been informed that M20 has a really good section helping people like me understand how to create and build your own magical paradigm, and I'm looking forward to getting my copy. As it is, I just run Mages as Sorcerers from Revised, only I let them have access to Blood Magic paths that run off Mana (Quintessance) ratther than Blood as well as the normal Hedge Magic paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 12-07-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:56:22-08:00","id":781773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781695#post781695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's easy enough. There's no reason the two can't co-exist side by side. In fact, one of the plot points for the Chronicle I made thise creatures for, is that one day Mikhail finds a way to &quot;upgrade&quot; existing Abominations into Strigoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>yup, that's my point, too :P<br /> they are cool, but this does not mean they should be the only Abominations around; a the group more diversified means a group less predictable, and this mean a way better narration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:00:45-08:00","id":781776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781773#post781773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yup, that's my point, too :P<br /> they are cool, but this does not mean they should be the only Abominations around; a the group more diversified means a group less predictable, and this mean a way better narration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:02:19-08:00","id":781861,"title":"","content":"I'm unclear why these things need to be Werewolves at all. They could just be a unique monster created from foul Thamauturgies applied to living things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:18:59-08:00","id":781873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781861#post781861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unclear why these things need to be Werewolves at all. They could just be a unique monster created from foul Thamauturgies applied to living things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply because I like the idea of a crossbred monstrosity that's appaling to both species. It's something that's antithetical to both and yet they can see themselves in it. A Dark Reflection if you will. <br /> <br /> What you're describing, is basically thaumaturgical Vozhd. We already have those. They're disturbing, yes, but ultimately, they're just a monster. I like the biggest terrors to not be the slathering beast but a reasoning creature capable of blending in, and interacting with those it threatens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:20:51-08:00","id":781877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781873#post781873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply because I like the idea of a crossbred monstrosity that's appaling to both species. It's something that's antithetical to both and yet they can see themselves in it. A Dark Reflection if you will.<br /> <br /> What you're describing, is basically thaumaturgical Vozhd. We already have those. They're disturbing, yes, but ultimately, they're just a monster. I like the biggest terrors to not be the slathering beast but a reasoning creature capable of blending in, and interacting with those it threatens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. Why does it have to be a Werewolf to be intelligent?. Outside the physicallity it brings absolutley nothing from Werwolf to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:15:59-08:00","id":781918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781877#post781877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again. Why does it have to be a Werewolf to be intelligent?. Outside the physicallity it brings absolutley nothing from Werwolf to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Gifts and Rites? The Personal Totem from a Wyrm Spirit? The shapeshifting, and the ability to walk in the spirit world? Yeah, its all there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:42:28-08:00","id":782169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=781918#post781918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the Gifts and Rites? The Personal Totem from a Wyrm Spirit? The shapeshifting, and the ability to walk in the spirit world? Yeah, its all there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all mechanical buffs. What does it offer on a spiritual and conceptual level? I could insert a cat or a human and give him the same powers and it would be the same monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T04:20:11-08:00","id":782216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782169#post782169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all mechanical buffs. What does it offer on a spiritual and conceptual level? I could insert a cat or a human and give him the same powers and it would be the same monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you Cog. Making it a Garou Vampire serves very little thematically other than making it 'special snowflakey'. As I've said again, if this is what you want and you're running a mixed WoD game and you want the PC Vampires to work with the PC Werewolves to kill this thing, and that'll be the start of diplomacy for the -next- adventure. Then fair enough.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's just a bit Samuel Haight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:09:50-08:00","id":782276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vorcen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782216#post782216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with you Cog. Making it a Garou Vampire serves very little thematically other than making it 'special snowflakey'. As I've said again, if this is what you want and you're running a mixed WoD game and you want the PC Vampires to work with the PC Werewolves to kill this thing, and that'll be the start of diplomacy for the -next- adventure. Then fair enough.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's just a bit Samuel Haight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, then it's not for you. Doesn't bother me any. Others liked the concept in another thread, and wanted me to share the details. I have done so. If you don't like, don't use it. That's why its an option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:11:59-08:00","id":782308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782276#post782276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, then it's not for you. Doesn't bother me any. Others liked the concept in another thread, and wanted me to share the details. I have done so. If you don't like, don't use it. That's why its an option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it's to make a fearsome and terrifying enemy right? On that note I remember house-ruling some unique powers to abomination NPCs to make them more powerful.<br /> <br /> Blood Gifts:<br /> <br /> Thanks to an Abominations unique background they are able to blend the the rituals and ritae of blood magic with the rites of the garou. this allows them to study and create unique gifts using the unholy blood.<br /> <br /> Rule's:<br /> <br /> An abomination must have a level in thaumaturgy equal or greater than the rank of the gift they wish to learn/create. Creating a gift hold the same rules as creating a thaum ritual.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Blood frenzy: rank 3 EXP 10<br /> <br /> An abomination knows the tainted power of blood and the force of the beast within, this gift allows one to focus the rage of the beast into spiritual rage to power their gifts.<br /> <br /> An abomination may spend one BP to gain one rage and vise versa. An abomination may not transfer more blood or rage per turn greater than half their dots of rage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Spiritual</span></span></span> vampire: Rank 5 EXP 15<br /> <br /> An abominations vampiric nature bleeds into it's more spiritual aspects, gaining them new powers all their own. Their claws and fangs cry out with their unnatural hunger, draining their foes of strength.<br /> <br /> Whenever an abomination deals damage with it's claw or bite attacks they drain one &quot;energy point&quot; from their targets highest pool(gnosis and rage from garou, blood for vampires, quintessence for mages). What energy is drained goes to the abominations corresponding pool, if the abomination doesn't have one(quintessence) then it's absorbed into blood. If the abominations pools are full then they energy is transferred to healing 1 point heals 1 level of lethal or bashing damage, 3 points to heal aggravated damage. any excess energy remaining by the end of the turn dissipates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:58:53-08:00","id":782329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782308#post782308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well it's to make a fearsome and terrifying enemy right? On that note I remember house-ruling some unique powers to abomination NPCs to make them more powerful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! I've wanted to do more &quot;crossover&quot; powers for the Abomination, but I'm honestly only mildly familiar with Werewolf the Apocalypse. I actually prefer Forsaken, at least as far as settings and theme go. I might borrow those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T11:09:07-08:00","id":782394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782329#post782329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting! I've wanted to do more &quot;crossover&quot; powers for the Abomination, but I'm honestly only mildly familiar with Werewolf the Apocalypse. I actually prefer Forsaken, at least as far as settings and theme go. I might borrow those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing unique to crossovers I personally love is(As my friend termed it) &quot;Mixed magic&quot;, like a mage and a thaumaturge working together on a ritual. The thaumaturge works the linear portion of the ritual and the mage amplifies the effects and lowers the difficulty. With the assistance of the mage the thaumaturges magic is easier and far more powerful, and with the thaumaturges rituals disguising his magic the mage can avoid paradox(not to mention the fact that amplifying a ritual that's already coincidental is probably far simpler than even performing a rote.)<br /> <br /> By merging two schools of magic, a person can merge two similar effects to make the outcome more powerful(as per mage example) or even create entirely new and unique abilities(as per the unique gifts of abominations). It's a concept that I personally adore playing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:06:43-08:00","id":782425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782394#post782394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One thing unique to crossovers I personally love is(As my friend termed it) &quot;Mixed magic&quot;, like a mage and a thaumaturge working together on a ritual. The thaumaturge works the linear portion of the ritual and the mage amplifies the effects and lowers the difficulty. With the assistance of the mage the thaumaturges magic is easier and far more powerful, and with the thaumaturges rituals disguising his magic the mage can avoid paradox(not to mention the fact that amplifying a ritual that's already coincidental is probably far simpler than even performing a rote.)<br /> <br /> By merging two schools of magic, a person can merge two similar effects to make the outcome more powerful(as per mage example) or even create entirely new and unique abilities(as per the unique gifts of abominations). It's a concept that I personally adore playing with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the original creation ritual for my breed of Abomination worked. A Hermetic Tremere mage led the research, but he had Cainite Tremere assistants. The reason why it can't be successfully replicated is that it requires True Magick and Blood Magic to work, and Mikhail doesn't understand that there's a difference. He's managed to successfully replicate the Thaumaturgical parts and just cant' understand why it keeps FAILING.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:48:08-08:00","id":782477,"title":"","content":"Interesting, but it seems like you've left something out. Maybe automatically getting a hot catsuit-clad vampire girlfriend who looks like Kate Beckinsale upon the character becoming an abomination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:39:25-08:00","id":782550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=782477#post782477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, but it seems like you've left something out. Maybe automatically getting a hot catsuit-clad vampire girlfriend who looks like Kate Beckinsale upon the character becoming an abomination?</div> </div> </div> </div>*LAUGHS* Not what I was going for, but that was one of my inspiration sources, yes. Along with Blade (different kind of Hybrid) and Klaus Mikaelson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T04:43:59-08:00","id":792095,"title":"","content":"I'm running a crossover game where players can assume the roles of abominations as well as Kindred, Garou, Mages and Fallen (We currently have 2 active abomination characters).<br /> <br /> Abominations can choose 2 Disciplines from their clan, 2 rank 1 Gifts from their Breed and 2 rank 1 Gifts from Auspice. They need blood just like Vampires do and they're sensitive to sunlight just like Vampires are. They can shapeshift in a deformed form of Lupus, Glabro, Hispo and Crinos. They're not that much hunted by other races though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:36:40-07:00","id":875260,"title":"","content":"Over the almost 2 decades i have had the books, the only real modification i myself came up with or Abominations was this.. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Abominations go by for the Under a Blood Red Moon book for rules and creation instructions. If an Abominations ever get put into the Umbral lake of Erebus, they will be cleansed of Wyrm taint in the same way as a Vampire will, but spends 300 years as a base and 1 century for every additional humanity point to be gained. If cause of this, they reach the state known as Golconda, they can choose to either Die and be reborn as a Garou (or other Fera) with a bonus of 2 Gnosis and Willpower. Or they can instantly regain their Garou state, but they do not gain any lost powers or Gnosis.</span></li> </ol><br /> Your rules seem decent enough for NPC only baddies (especially since all their were gifts have to come from the dark/baddie spirits etc)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:56:09-07:00","id":932603,"title":"","content":"I admit, I briefly considered revising Abomination Rules myself. The result was less than &quot;Godlike&quot; though.<br /> <br /> * A werewolf embraced by a vampire loses all of its connection to Gaia.<br /> * It instead gains Protean as an Additional Clan Discipline and the ability to assume a Crinos seeming &quot;War Form&quot; with the 5th level instead of Mist.<br /> * They have the Road of the Beast instead of Humanity.<br /> * They have the Brujah flaw in addition to any other Clan flaw.<br /> * Only Banes and coerced spirits obey it if they learn Spirit Thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T15:27:58-07:00","id":932652,"title":"","content":"Without the flaws of either species, these Abominations feel like neither of them. They just feel like twinked out death machines, so where's the story potential? For me, silver and sunlight are an inescapable trope of both monsters. Sunlight, especially, adds to the themes of vampirism--if you're forced to only ever live by night, there's something very tragic about that. If you add in vulnerabilities to silver, sunlight and fire, then, you suddenly have something that feels like both creatures.<br /> <br /> TBH, I think a more interesting idea would be to come up with a monster that mimicked the monstrous werewolf Wamphyri of the Necroscope books. Now that would be an interesting werewolf-vampire hybrid to throw at PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T07:38:59-07:00","id":932898,"title":"","content":"It ALIIIIIIVE!<br /> <br /> Sorry I always want to say that when an old thread suddenly revives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:37:15-07:00","id":934506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=875260#post875260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your rules seem decent enough for NPC only baddies (especially since all their were gifts have to come from the dark/baddie spirits etc)...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they're meant to be, and why I front=loaded so many advisories and warnings. These are meant to function in one of two capacities: as a long term Big Bad, or as the Michael Meyers of the WtA/VtM. I knew when I posted it, I'd see people crying &quot;OP&quot; and &quot;god characters&quot; and completely miss the point of it. It's also not for everyone. I personally grew tired of crapsack worlds years ago, where everyone sucks, the world is slouching towards oblivion, and nothing matters. <br /> <br /> Now, I use the Storyteller System to do Urban Fantasy games closer in tone to the Dresden Files or Nightside than the classic World of Darkness nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 07-20-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:33:49-07:00","id":934649,"title":"","content":"I don't see why you stated that they lost their Gifts they knew. That is like saying that someone who gains the ability to use artillery instantly learns how to fire a glock. I am wondering how that is justified? Mind you, I like the idea. I am just asking for clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:48:58-07:00","id":934693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=934649#post934649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why you stated that they lost their Gifts they knew. That is like saying that someone who gains the ability to use artillery instantly learns how to fire a glock. I am wondering how that is justified? Mind you, I like the idea. I am just asking for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was under the impression a werewolf lost access to gifts if their Totem shunned them or they became Wyrm-taint. If I'm wrong, I'll amend that. I haven't read a Werewolf core book in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:10:58-07:00","id":934866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781297-alternate-take-on-abominations?p=934693#post934693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was under the impression a werewolf lost access to gifts if their Totem shunned them or they became Wyrm-taint. If I'm wrong, I'll amend that. I haven't read a Werewolf core book in a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>not typically, but it wouldn't be unprecedented.<br /> easy enough to rationalize though as the spirit half being rended during the embrace and that's why they lose gifts, assuming you want that to be an effect of the embrace. surviving the embrace should be a harrowing experience for any half-spirit creature and so any aftereffects you want can be attributed to that part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:51:29-07:00","id":936257,"title":"","content":"The problem that they have is they start losing permanent Gnosis and cannot get it back. I do not use the Ego rules and just rule that they stop being Abominations and just become normal vampires with an interesting back story if they ever reach Gnosis 0. I also treat them as a Kinfolk and let them use any level 1 Gift that does not require Gnosis or Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-23-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}